==Trivia== 
*The word "''Archer''" comes from the Latin "''arcus''", meaning bow. The practice of archery was first developed in Africa by the later Middle Stone Age (approx. 70,000 years ago). It is documented as part of warfare and hunting from the classical period until the late medieval period when it was made obsolete by the increased use of firearms.
**The bow that Archers use in [[Basics of Battle|battle]] is a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recurve_bow recurve bow].
**The Archers are 1 of 10 [[cards]] associated with archery, with the others being the [[Arrows]], [[Tower Princess]], [[X-Bow]], [[Princess]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Super Archers]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
***The Archers, Arrows, and Tower Princess are the only cards associated with archery that are unlocked in [[Training Camp]].
*The Archers are 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being the [[Minions]], [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the Archer Queen.
**The Archers resemble the Level 1 Archer from Clash of Clans. Their [[Star Points|Star Level 2 skin]] grants them a tiara similar to the Level 7 Archer in Clash of Clans.
**Archers in Clash Royale share a similar deploy sound effect with their Clash of Clans counterpart.
**In Clash of Clans, the Archers' movement speed is high, whereas in Clash Royale, their movement speed is moderate.
*The Archers are 1 of 7 cards that are already unlocked for the player when they start playing the game, the others being the Minions, [[Knight]], Arrows, Tower Princess, Giant, and [[Fireball]]. Despite this, the game recognizes that those cards are unlocked in the Training Camp.
*The Archers are one of the first troop cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Minions, Knight, [[Spear Goblins]], Goblins, [[Bomber]], Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], Witch, P.E.K.K.A, [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The Archers are one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A., Prince, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], Magic Archer, [[Bandit]], Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*Even though the card spawns 2 Archers, the card render displays only 1 Archer.
*From the [[Firecracker]]'s description, it is implied that the Firecracker used to be an Archer.
*It's unknown why the Archers have a small pouch on her belt, though it's most likely there to store supplies, such as bowstrings and water.
*Despite wearing a quiver filled with arrows, the Archers don't take the arrows out of her quiver when performing an attack.
*In [[Pass Royale|Fisherman's Float]], Shipwreck Island, and Island Arena, Archers can be seen sitting in the audience.
*The Archers are featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Archers, along with the Goblins, Barbarians, [[Elite Barbarians]], and P.E.K.K.A., were featured as a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Monster monster] in [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Puzzle_%26_Dragons_Wiki Puzzles and Dragons], in a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Dungeon dungeon] called [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Clash_of_Clans_Dungeon Clash of Clans Dungeon].
**The Archers, along with the Goblins, Barbarians, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Battle Healer]], Witch, Miner, Ice Wizard, and Bandit, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squaddies Squaddie] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Archers, along with the Goblins, Barbarians, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A., Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, Prince, and Night Witch, are featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater]. Also, along with the Goblins, Skeletons, Barbarians, Mini P.E.K.K.A., Musketeer, Wizard, Witch, Prince, and Princess, they are featured in the [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama] sticker pack.
*The Archers are the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Archers are the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
***The [https://clashroyale.fandom.com/wiki/Emotes?file=Slowmo_Archer.png Archer Slowmo Emote] is a reference to Clash Royale's [https://youtu.be/TJryIc0Cwy4?si=5lN2tWZ-xNBMjHee The Last Second commercial].
**The Archers are the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
**The Archers are the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Deadly Trio decoration was created by [https://x.com/suzyq53936155 SuzyQ].
*The Archers were featured in the winning decks of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Archers were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VxEzjdKQ4HA Clash Royale Helsinki Tournament], by a player called Jason.
**The Archers were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/1fuCnNBTqBU?feature=share King's Cup Tournament], by a player called TMD YAOYAO.
**The Archers were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kIGdeKaT_is The Crown Duel Tournament], by a player called Backstabx.

